{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e","id":832433,"title":"Why Call Them Kiths and Seemings in 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-18T03:58:06-08:00","id":832433,"title":"Why Call Them Kiths and Seemings in 2E?","content":"One thing I don't get about Changleing 2E is that it completely changes what Kiths and Seemings are, yet still keeps the names, which now seem really awkward. Don't get me wrong, I'm not complaining about what Kiths and Seemings have been turned into. In fact, I really love the changes as they truly encapsulate a changeling's nature, it's just that the changes should come full circle into new names for the new concepts.<br /> <br /> Seeming suggests something that is an outward appearance that is deceptive in nature, which makes sense for what it was in 1E. But in 2E, the Seeming reflects what the changeling did, not what their Keeper did. Kith means neighbors, friends, or other relationships that aren't as close as family but closer than acquaintances, which worked for what they were in 1E, but not for what they are in 2E. Perhaps the term Seeming could replace Kith (that would make sense since Seeming in 1E was what the Keeper turned the changeling into) and Abandon could replace Seeming (it's related as both a verb and noun).<br /> <br /> On that note, perhaps some of the Seemings themselves should also go through name changes. I can see Elemental, Ogre, Fairest, and Wizened, considering their ties to fairy tales and how they relate so well to how they break from their Keepers, but ones like Darkling and Beast don't make much sense in the new context (to me, at least). Again, not that the concepts for them are bad, just that the names don't suit, which isn't surprising when you consider what they were originally crafted for.<br /> <br /> But maybe I'm missing something here, what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T04:17:51-08:00","id":832437,"title":"","content":"Kith is like family, and just like how you you don't pick your family you don't get to pick your kith. Your kith also gives you advantages from your body, that might not fit with your characters personality or interests, but they still get the advantages, sorta like genetics... which you generally get from your family.<br /> <br /> And seeming is specifically what determines how you look. All beasts will look animalistic. All elementals will look composed of some sort of material. But, the seeming is decided by only a single (but major) moment in the changelings life, so it can be deceptive. You can't trust a fairest just because he looks like a protagonist. Darklings are not always dishonest despite being permanently tainted by their act of betrayal.<br /> <br /> As for beast and darkling themselves. How is &quot;Defies societies rules because I'm of beast not of man&quot; not fit the name of Beast... also they all look like animals. As for darklings, they are defined by having committing the dark and sinister act of betrayal as a characters Defining moment in the eyes of the wyrd. Darklings are individuals who the wyrd will always see as someone who commited an act of &quot;evil&quot;. The darkling is the evil guy you know is evil in a movie because he's always hiding in the shadows, speaks with a raspy voice and omnious music starts playing when they are on the screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-18-2016, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:40:03-08:00","id":832676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832437#post832437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kith is like family, and just like how you you don't pick your family you don't get to pick your kith. Your kith also gives you advantages from your body, that might not fit with your characters personality or interests, but they still get the advantages, sorta like genetics... which you generally get from your family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing kith with kin. Kin is family, kith is friends and neighbors. After all, the saying goes &quot;next of kin&quot;, not &quot;next of kith&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832437#post832437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And seeming is specifically what determines how you look. All beasts will look animalistic. All elementals will look composed of some sort of material. But, the seeming is decided by only a single (but major) moment in the changelings life, so it can be deceptive. You can't trust a fairest just because he looks like a protagonist. Darklings are not always dishonest despite being permanently tainted by their act of betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It goes much further than mere aesthetic. That, and the whole theme behind Seeming is how a changeling broke free into reality, and we're gonna use a term that suggests deception? It provides the context of their Clarity, so how on earth does that even begin to relate to illusion? It seems more like the opposite of illusion. Also, just because a Seeming can be deceptive doesn't mean it always is. Deception is not the core of the concept, so it shouldn't be named after it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832437#post832437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for beast and darkling themselves. How is &quot;Defies societies rules because I'm of beast not of man&quot; not fit the name of Beast... also they all look like animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, maybe I'm getting hung up on how Beasts in 1E were literally turned into animal-like creatures, and for the context to change so drastically, it seems inappropriate to call them Beasts to me. Not to mention there's an entire template that shares the same name that also exists in dreams, so there's that as well. Perhaps Primals would work better, as they don't look like animals so much as they look animalistic..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832437#post832437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for darklings, they are defined by having committing the dark and sinister act of betrayal as a characters Defining moment in the eyes of the wyrd. Darklings are individuals who the wyrd will always see as someone who commited an act of &quot;evil&quot;. The darkling is the evil guy you know is evil in a movie because he's always hiding in the shadows, speaks with a raspy voice and omnious music starts playing when they are on the screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't Villains be a more appropriate term, then? Why should they be constrained to the dark? Evil is everywhere, and a common trope is how villains can appear to be the hero or innocent at first before showing their true nature. Certainly not all Darklings are bad people, but they are defined by a moment where they abandoned some sense of morality to escape, thus looking like the bad guy in the Wyrd's eyes as you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T14:53:42-08:00","id":832770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832676#post832676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're confusing kith with kin. Kin is family, kith is friends and neighbors. After all, the saying goes &quot;next of kin&quot;, not &quot;next of kith&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going off <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/kith\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> definition of kith, which includes relatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It goes much further than mere aesthetic. That, and the whole theme behind Seeming is how a changeling broke free into reality, and we're gonna use a term that suggests deception? It provides the context of their Clarity, so how on earth does that even begin to relate to illusion? It seems more like the opposite of illusion. Also, just because a Seeming can be deceptive doesn't mean it always is. Deception is not the core of the concept, so it shouldn't be named after it. </div> </div> </div>It goes further than aesthetic, but only in &quot;we give you additional things that match this aesthetic&quot;... As for deception. Seeming doesn't mean DECEPTION! it means, the external appearance as distinguished from true character. Seeming is what the wyrd thinks you are. You saved people and sacrificed yourself, so the wyrd makes you look like a hero... But that doesn't Make you a hero. One act does not reflect who you truly are. Seemings are deceptive in 2e... at least, more deceptive than they were in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dunno, maybe I'm getting hung up on how Beasts in 1E were literally turned into animal-like creatures, and for the context to change so drastically, it seems inappropriate to call them Beasts to me. Not to mention there's an entire template that shares the same name that also exists in dreams, so there's that as well. Perhaps Primals would work better, as they don't look like animals so much as they look animalistic.. </div> </div> </div>.... So you can't call the beasts because.... they are only bestial. Look at them. They're beasts. Have you looked at the beast from beauty and the beast? That's what beasts look like and why they named the way they are. You don't need to be 100% animal to be a beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't Villains be a more appropriate term, then? Why should they be constrained to the dark? Evil is everywhere, and a common trope is how villains can appear to be the hero or innocent at first before showing their true nature. Certainly not all Darklings are bad people, but they are defined by a moment where they abandoned some sense of morality to escape, thus looking like the bad guy in the Wyrd's eyes as you said. </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be a villain to betray someone. In many tales dark characters end up betraying people regrettably or because they are being manipulated by the villain. Also, calling darklings villains would be like renaming Fairest as Heroes, it lacks the fey sounding aesthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T14:54:41-08:00","id":832771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832676#post832676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Villains be a more appropriate term, then? Why should they be constrained to the dark? Evil is everywhere, and a common trope is how villains can appear to be the hero or innocent at first before showing their true nature. Certainly not all Darklings are bad people, but they are defined by a moment where they abandoned some sense of morality to escape, thus looking like the bad guy in the Wyrd's eyes as you said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always saw the original 6 Seemings as 3 sets of parallels/mirrors:<br /> <br /> Beasts are the living, moving part of Nature; Elementals are the rest of Nature.<br /> <br /> Wizened are made smaller by their Durance; Ogres are made larger.<br /> <br /> To a Medieval European, particularly those of the British Isles from which much Changeling Lore is derived, Fairest didn't just mean &quot;most just&quot;, or &quot;most honest&quot;, it also meant palest or lightest; &quot;Snow White&quot;, for example. So Darklings are the opposite; they are shadowed, swarthy, and in the minds of a Medieval European, sinister. Racist? Yeah, a little, but the Gentry are set in their ways, and apparently so is the Wyrd.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 02-18-2016, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T15:21:09-08:00","id":832787,"title":"","content":"Frankly I think True Fae would find the notion that some humans think they're better than other humans because they have less skin pigment hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:02:15-08:00","id":832807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832787#post832787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I think True Fae would find the notion that some humans think they're better than other humans because they have less skin pigment hilarious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discrimination and oppression for frequently superficial reasons is at the heart of a great deal of human stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:12:10-08:00","id":832809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832770#post832770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going off <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/kith\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> definition of kith, which includes relatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keyword here being <i>include</i>. Relatives are only a single part of the main definition, so my point still stands. Kin is more appropriate to the argument you're making.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832770#post832770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It goes further than aesthetic, but only in &quot;we give you additional things that match this aesthetic&quot;... As for deception. Seeming doesn't mean DECEPTION! it means, the external appearance as distinguished from true character. Seeming is what the wyrd thinks you are. You saved people and sacrificed yourself, so the wyrd makes you look like a hero... But that doesn't Make you a hero. One act does not reflect who you truly are. Seemings are deceptive in 2e... at least, more deceptive than they were in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say Seeming meant deception, I said it <i>suggests</i> deception. Yes, Seeming is defined as an outward appearance that is different to true character, and right there we see how Seeming doesn't work as a term. Seeming is being used for something that is, if anything, the true character of a changeling, as it's defined by what the changeling did to Arcadia. It reflects the utter desperation the changeling had to escape, whether they were willing to abandon civility, dignity, morality, or whatever else in order to do it. Yes, it's one act, but it's a very revealing one. Like the Joker said &quot;In their last moments, people show you who they really are...&quot;. Complete desperation, like trying to escape from a torturous and confusing (at best) world, does very much the same thing as inevitable death.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the fact that Seeming is made to be a character defining trait in both theme and mechanics of the game. The term was fine in 1E as it specifically related to what the Keeper made the changeling into, which didn't truly reflect their character necessarily. But now that Seeming is used for what the changeling did to escape, it's not so good a term.<br /> <br /> This is why I suggested Abandon. As a verb, it reflects the escape, they're abandoning the role they play in their Keeper's sick game. As a noun, it reflects their unfettering behavior, they escape with a desperate abandon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832770#post832770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... So you can't call the beasts because.... they are only bestial. Look at them. They're beasts. Have you looked at the beast from beauty and the beast? That's what beasts look like and why they named the way they are. You don't need to be 100% animal to be a beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't necessarily have to look like beasts. Seeming in 2E has nothing to do with outward appearance so much as it reflects what they did to escape. In other words, Seeming only <i>affects</i> a changeling's appearance, it in and of itself is not an appearance. Also, let's consider the other Beasts as well. Y'know, the ones that are said to be family to changelings (which really throws the term Kith for a loop when you think about it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832770#post832770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to be a villain to betray someone. In many tales dark characters end up betraying people regrettably or because they are being manipulated by the villain. Also, calling darklings villains would be like renaming Fairest as Heroes, it lacks the fey sounding aesthetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but you also don't have to be dark to abandon the moral high ground (see what I did there?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832771#post832771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw the original 6 Seemings as 3 sets of parallels/mirrors:<br /> <br /> Beasts are the living, moving part of Nature; Elementals are the rest of Nature.<br /> <br /> Wizened are made smaller by their Durance; Ogres are made larger.<br /> <br /> To a Medieval European, particularly those of the British Isles from which much Changeling Lore is derived, Fairest didn't just mean &quot;most just&quot;, or &quot;most honest&quot;, it also meant palest or lightest; &quot;Snow White&quot;, for example. So Darklings are the opposite; they are shadowed, swarthy, and in the minds of a Medieval European, sinister. Racist? Yeah, a little, but the Gentry are set in their ways, and apparently so is the Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much racist as it is limiting, as abandoning morality would be more akin to evil in a story sense than dark necessarily. Then again, one could say the same about Fairest and it's only really a nitpick at most. I still think Beast should be changed though, if anything just to alleviate confusion with another game that's designed for crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:17:40-08:00","id":832813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seeming in 2E has nothing to do with outward appearance so much as it reflects what they did to escape. </div> </div> </div>*Looks at how seeming is the primary thing that determines your appearance and overrides your kith's appearance*<br /> Uh... what?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's true, but you also don't have to be dark to abandon the moral high ground (see what I did there?). </div> </div> </div>... when you abandon the moral high ground it's called descending into darkness... so no....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:34:50-08:00","id":832822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832813#post832813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Looks at how seeming is the primary thing that determines your appearance and overrides your kith's appearance*<br /> Uh... what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at it this way: There's a fighter. They get into a lot of fights, and as a result are peppered with scars, scabs, and bruises. When others look at them, they see a fighter. Does that mean fighter is their appearance? No, that's makes absolutely no sense. Being a fighter has nothing to do with appearance, though being a fighter affects one's appearance. A person may have a fighter's appearance, but fighter in and of itself is not an appearance, it reflects one's actions and choices in life, the appearance is merely a consequence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832813#post832813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... when you abandon the moral high ground it's called descending into darkness... so no....</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just a saying, you don't literally descend into darkness when you abandon morality. It may be a common trope for those who abandon morals to be dark, but there's another common trope that defies it (wolf in sheep's clothing), and another one that subverts it (dark is not evil).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:38:37-08:00","id":832824,"title":"","content":"A seeming is more than just an appearance. It's the archetype by which a changeling reforged their humanoid form. Metaphor and literal reality are entwined together like a braid for the fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:53:39-08:00","id":832835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">A seeming is more than just an appearance. It's the archetype by which a changeling reforged their humanoid form. Metaphor and literal reality are entwined together like a braid for the fae.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It is definitely more than just appearance. What I was refuting was that &quot;</span><i>Seeming in 2E has nothing to do with outward appearance&quot; </i>which is blatantly false.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look at it this way: There's a fighter. They get into a lot of fights, and as a result are peppered with scars, scabs, and bruises. When others look at them, they see a fighter. Does that mean fighter is their appearance? No, that's makes absolutely no sense. Being a fighter has nothing to do with appearance, though being a fighter affects one's appearance. A person may have a fighter's appearance, but fighter in and of itself is not an appearance, it reflects one's actions and choices in life, the appearance is merely a consequence. </div> </div> </div>But that fighter-ness would be the persons kith rather than their seeming in this situation. The seeming, literally changes their appearance to fit a specific theme, which is informed by the kith. Okay, the guy was a fighter so he might be a Bloodbrute (might be misremembering the name of the kith). But then you add the seeming on the top which could make the changeling look like a wolverine (beast), a man who has armour replacing his lost limbs (wizened), a women made from hardened ice (elemental), a giantess covered in never healing scars (ogre), etc. The seeming greatly affects the appearance. It defines the appearance, both in the changelings mein and in the eyes of the wyrd.<br /> <br /> edit: It's really easy to guess a changelings seeming through appearance because of how much the seeming defines the appearance, but kiths... they are harder to guess. Could you guess the kiths of the following changelings: a changeling who looks like a humanoid chameleon, a changeling who looks like a living puddle, and a gaunt and twisted changeling that has many anguished/pained faces along his flesh? But telling their seemings is easy, beast/elemental/darkling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's just a saying, you don't literally descend into darkness when you abandon morality </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just a saying&quot; is a foolish thing to think in a game that runs on narrative tropes.....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It may be a common trope for those who abandon morals to be dark, but there's another common trope that defies it (wolf in sheep's clothing), and another one that subverts it (dark is not evil). </div> </div> </div>1. Dark is not evil is a trope only because Dark = Evil is a bigger trope. As you say, it subverts it.<br /> 2. The defying the trope is why it's called Seeming. Because it can be defied, easily. &quot;You can't trust a fairest just because he looks like a protagonist. Darklings are not always dishonest despite being permanently tainted by their act of betrayal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-18-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T17:37:57-08:00","id":832869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832835#post832835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It is definitely more than just appearance. What I was refuting was that &quot;</span><i>Seeming in 2E has nothing to do with outward appearance&quot; </i>which is blatantly false.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, Seeming is not defined by appearance, but by actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832835#post832835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that fighter-ness would be the persons kith rather than their seeming in this situation. The seeming, literally changes their appearance to fit a specific theme, which is informed by the kith. Okay, the guy was a fighter so he might be a Bloodbrute (might be misremembering the name of the kith). But then you add the seeming on the top which could make the changeling look like a wolverine (beast), a man who has armour replacing his lost limbs (wizened), a women made from hardened ice (elemental), a giantess covered in never healing scars (ogre), etc. The seeming greatly affects the appearance. It defines the appearance, both in the changelings mein and in the eyes of the wyrd.<br /> <br /> edit: It's really easy to guess a changelings seeming through appearance because of how much the seeming defines the appearance, but kiths... they are harder to guess. Could you guess the kiths of the following changelings: a changeling who looks like a humanoid chameleon, a changeling who looks like a living puddle, and a gaunt and twisted changeling that has many anguished/pained faces along his flesh? But telling their seemings is easy, beast/elemental/darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, fighter-ness is not the Kith, you're not listening to the actual argument being made. My point is: Being a fighter only affects your appearance, it is not an appearance itself. Being a fighter means you fight. Being a Darkling means you abandoned the moral high ground to escape. Darkling is not an appearance itself, it only accents it, colors it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832835#post832835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Just a saying&quot; is a foolish thing to think in a game that runs on narrative tropes.....</div> </div> </div> </div>And where do you think the tropes that go against Dark = Evil come from, exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832835#post832835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Dark is not evil is a trope only because Dark = Evil is a bigger trope. As you say, it subverts it.<br /> 2. The defying the trope is why it's called Seeming. Because it can be defied, easily. &quot;You can't trust a fairest just because he looks like a protagonist. Darklings are not always dishonest despite being permanently tainted by their act of betrayal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) And what do you suppose are the bigger tropes, True Fae or changelings? Just sayin'.<br /> <br /> 2.) That argument makes no sense considering that Seeming is defined by the actions and choices a changeling made to escape, not what they appear to be. You wouldn't trust a Darkling because you know they'd betray any trust to escape. You can rely on a Fairest because you know they'll become a hero to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:38:00-08:00","id":832926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nope, Seeming is not defined by appearance, but by actions </div> </div> </div>I think this is why there is an issue in communication, since I did not say seeming is defined by appearance. At all. I'm said seeming defines the changelings appearance. Those are two completely different things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, fighter-ness is not the Kith, you're not listening to the actual argument being made. My point is: Being a fighter only affects your appearance, it is not an appearance itself. Being a fighter means you fight. Being a Darkling means you abandoned the moral high ground to escape. Darkling is not an appearance itself, it only accents it, colors it. </div> </div> </div>Ugh... No darkling is not an appearance itself. No single thing in existence is an appearance itself. That doesn't change the fact that seeming directly affects appearance in a major way, in a way that gives people perceptions of your character and views, regardless of whether they are appropriate in general. A darkling abandoned the moral high ground to escape, which gives people the automatic impression that they are untrustworthy in general. But that may have been the only time they ever betrayed anyone in their entire life and it haunts them that they did such a horrible thing. A beast broke the social conventions to escape, but that does not mean that breaking social conventions is something that character does all the time, they might have only done it because they were at breaking point. When in a traumatic situation, you can end up doing things that you would not normally do from a combination of being mentally broken and desperation. That is the seeming. It's an outer layer that everyone sees, but it may be deceptive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And where do you think the tropes that go against Dark = Evil come from, exactly? </div> </div> </div>I was actually just saying that because &quot;that's just a saying&quot; is a strange thing to say in a game were you were kidnapped by living stories. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">1.) And what do you suppose are the bigger tropes, True Fae or changelings? Just sayin'.[</span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">2.) That argument makes no sense considering that Seeming is defined by the actions and choices a changeling made to escape, not what they appear to be. You wouldn't trust a Darkling because you know they'd betray any trust to escape. You can rely on a Fairest because you know they'll become a hero to escape.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> 1) Sincerely don't know what your talking about. <br /> 2) Seeming is defined by the actions a changeling made in their escape. But it turns out that a single event does not necessarily reflect your entire life. The seeming reflects the individual during a pivotal immensely moment in the eyes of the wyrd. But one event does not automatically accurate describe your life before nor after that event. Darklings wont necessarily betray Any trust to escape, you just know that they have betrayed someone during there escape. You making the assumption that darklings shouldn't be trusted is Proof the term seeming is appropriate since your making assumptions based on their seeming alone. Your basically looking at a changeling, seeing they look creepy and gaunt and evil, and deciding that they are untrustworthy even if that changeling might be ridiculously trustworthy because of how much guilt he feels over the betrayal he enacted and is trying to eternally redeem himself and maybe even try to get the guy he betrayed out of Arcadia.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:31:00-08:00","id":832955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832926#post832926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is why there is an issue in communication, since I did not say seeming is defined by appearance. At all. I'm said seeming defines the changelings appearance. Those are two completely different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't define the changeling's appearance either, only affects it. So, point still stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832926#post832926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh... No darkling is not an appearance itself. No single thing in existence is an appearance itself. That doesn't change the fact that seeming directly affects appearance in a major way, in a way that gives people perceptions of your character and views, regardless of whether they are appropriate in general. A darkling abandoned the moral high ground to escape, which gives people the automatic impression that they are untrustworthy in general. But that may have been the only time they ever betrayed anyone in their entire life and it haunts them that they did such a horrible thing. A beast broke the social conventions to escape, but that does not mean that breaking social conventions is something that character does all the time, they might have only done it because they were at breaking point. When in a traumatic situation, you can end up doing things that you would not normally do from a combination of being mentally broken and desperation. That is the seeming. It's an outer layer that everyone sees, but it may be deceptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this is the core of your misunderstanding: Seeming is what you're given upon escape.<br /> <br /> No, that's not it. Seeming is what a changeling makes themselves into when escaping. It's their statement that they're not gonna take it anymore, a mark of them taking matters into their own hands, the transformation they undergo in order to take the pen that writes their story. That's why it's related to their Clarity. To say that the Wyrd gives it to them without any impact from them harms the underlying theme, its purpose in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832926#post832926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually just saying that because &quot;that's just a saying&quot; is a strange thing to say in a game were you were kidnapped by living stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not when you're talking about common tropes being defied or subverted, and that's what my whole argument against the term Darkling is based on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832926#post832926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Sincerely don't know what your talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you were going on about how Dark = Evil is a bigger trope than Dark =/= Evil, and in a game where you become part story and try to elude living stories, who do you think is going to be the bigger trope here? Changelings are underdogs by nature as they're trying to get away from Cthulhu-esque beings. Changelings are gonna be the ones subverting tropes to get away if anything, not falling into them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832926#post832926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Seeming is defined by the actions a changeling made in their escape. But it turns out that a single event does not necessarily reflect your entire life. The seeming reflects the individual during a pivotal immensely moment in the eyes of the wyrd. But one event does not automatically accurate describe your life before nor after that event. Darklings wont necessarily betray Any trust to escape, you just know that they have betrayed someone during there escape. You making the assumption that darklings shouldn't be trusted is Proof the term seeming is appropriate since your making assumptions based on their seeming alone. Your basically looking at a changeling, seeing they look creepy and gaunt and evil, and deciding that they are untrustworthy even if that changeling might be ridiculously trustworthy because of how much guilt he feels over the betrayal he enacted and is trying to eternally redeem himself and maybe even try to get the guy he betrayed out of Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, now that misunderstanding is on me. Tone can't be portrayed by literal text. When I was saying Darklings can't be trusted and Fairest can wasn't really what I myself was saying but rather the reasoning say, a Hedgefresh changeling might have. I apologize for the confusion.<br /> <br /> I also see your point in that a Seeming could indeed deceive, but that's not what defines a Seeming. That's like saying a fighter must have scars, scabs, and bruises. No, a fighter is defined as someone who fights, not someone who has scars, scabs, and bruises. They only have those as a consequence of fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 02-18-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:16:48-08:00","id":832975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/832433-why-call-them-kiths-and-seemings-in-2e?p=832955#post832955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not when you're talking about common tropes being defied or subverted, and that's what my whole argument against the term Darkling is based on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument is a lot of babble about tropes to try and argue that the typically straightforward aesthetic shorthand fairy tales use ought to be irrelevant to those elements of a character that specifically come from their interaction with a force that runs on (for lack of a more accurate concise term) fairy tale logic in the course of their effective escape-by-rebirth out of the cauldron of myth where that force is at its strongest.<br /> <br /> An individual Darkling could walk the straight and narrow until the day they die, but the Wyrd still stamps the signs of their betrayal into their mien as part of the unspoken promise that ends their Durance. It doesn't matter how they've acted since Arcadia, they look creepy/suspicious/obfuscated because those are the marks of a Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T20:18:48-08:00","id":832977,"title":"","content":"Of course, they could go on a journey to shed their Seeming. But that's supplemental material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}